{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Interpretation 1</b><br>דופק [knocking]. Like מתדפקים על הדלת [knocking on the door], and דופק refers back to דודי, not to קול [voice] — like קול דודי [the voice of my beloved]: הנה זה בא [here he comes]." "קווצותי. The ends of the hair [and it is inverted]." "רסיסי. With it רביבים [drops], and like it לרוס את הסלת [to crush the fine flour]." "<b>Interpretation 2</b><br>And behold, she saw in a dream the image of her beloved, and said: אני ישנה [I am asleep] — even though I am asleep, לבי ער [my heart is awake], and I saw as though דודי [my beloved] came." "קול דודי דופק [the voice of my beloved is knocking] — for שראשי נמלא טל [my head is filled with dew] [בחוץ] [outside], and behold he was delayed a little, and I said in my heart: I have removed my garment. And my soul went out at his word to me. [ו]הנה אלך לדרכי [I will go my way] because you delayed. And upon waking she said: השבעתי [I adjure you] — what will you tell him? Tell him: חולת אהבה אני [I am faint with love]." "<b>Interpretation 3</b><br>אני ישנה [I am asleep]. Congregation of Israel said: even though I was exiled to Babylon, לבי ער [my heart is awake] and I did not serve idols." "קול דודי דופק [the voice of my beloved is knocking]. Through the prophets, that they should rebuild the Temple and go forth from Babylon." "שראשי נמלא טל קווצותי רסיסי לילה [for my head is filled with dew, my locks with drops of the night]. From the tears of [Congregation of] Israel — כענין בכה תבכה בלילה [as in: weep, weep in the night]."], :book :song-of-songs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {4 "The bracketed reading interpolates narrative connective tissue; translated hyper-literally as the textual state requires."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra's commentary on the Canticles" "http://beta.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH002030344/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:44:27.676310396Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}